// Q9 – Debugging the Event Loop

/*
PREDICTED OUTPUT (before running):
  1. Script start
  2. Script end
  3. Promise callback
  4. Timeout callback
*/

console.log("Script start");
setTimeout(() => console.log("Timeout callback"), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log("Promise callback"));
console.log("Script end");

/*
ACTUAL OUTPUT (matches prediction):
  Script start
  Script end
  Promise callback
  Timeout callback

EXPLANATION:
- Synchronous code ("Script start", "Script end") runs first on the call stack.
- setTimeout schedules a MACROtask; Promise.then schedules a MICROtask.
- When the stack empties, the event loop runs ALL microtasks before moving to
  the next macrotask. So "Promise callback" runs before "Timeout callback",
  even though the timer delay is 0 ms.
*/